WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.840
Speaker 1: David.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.660
How can Democrats better appeal to rural voters?

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:12.570
So I don't know if this will be seen as controversial
by people in my audience, but a lot of Democratic

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.180
rhetoric on gun control is completely counterproductive.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:24.690
I am probably right there with 95 percent
of the policy that many Democratic lawmakers

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.900
want on gun safety.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:35.120
But every time that Democrats campaign on
gun control, no one many sound very uninformed,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.350
very, very uninformed words like do they do
they even understand how guns work?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.059
And that's a real problem for a huge part
of this country, including rural folks who

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:45.040
remember rural folks.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.110
Relationship to guns is very different than
that of people who live in cities and suburbs

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.050
and other places.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:01:00.809
Number two, I think that the focus needs to
better emphasize economic issues in a way

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:09.979
that relates to working class may be better
than sort of like tech millennials.

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:17.529
And I think that sometimes the economic rhetoric
of Democrats works pretty well for young people

00:01:17.529 --> 00:01:21.580
and people working in white collar jobs, but
who are just not paid that well or with a

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:30.560
lot of student debt, but often is not rhetoric
and language that's well tuned to more rural

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.560
folks.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.610
And this includes farmers.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.109
This includes factory workers.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:39.419
And, you know, just every once in a while
talking about unions, there's lots of rural

00:01:39.419 --> 00:01:41.179
folks who have.

00:01:41.179 --> 00:01:46.590
One local employer where you drive 40 miles
to a factory where we might think being on

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:52.179
the left, they should love to hear about how
we support unionization, look at what happened

00:01:52.179 --> 00:01:55.299
in Alabama with Amazon, where they voted against
unionizing.

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:59.469
Now, of course, there was a huge propaganda
war and it's a much more complicated thing.

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:05.319
But having spoken to people who work in factories
in the Midwest and in other places, just talking

00:02:05.319 --> 00:02:07.559
about unions is not going to do it for Democrats.

00:02:07.559 --> 00:02:10.469
So I think that it's sort of a three pronged
approach.

00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:15.450
I think the rhetoric around gun control around
elections has to be either dropped or fixed.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.000
It doesn't mean you stop working on the issues.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.040
It just means you stop campaigning so aggressively
on that because it turns a lot of those rural

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.040
folks off.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:28.150
Number two, you figure out how to better talk
to farmers and agricultural employers and

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.409
workers.

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:38.659
And number three, you tweak the economic message
to not be so union heavy, but more about understanding

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:44.189
the plight of a lot of these economically
ravaged areas where whether the one employer

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:51.040
is unionized or not and I support the unionization,
that's not a path to fixing or dealing with

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.370
the way that the area has been ravaged.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:58.799
Big picture overwhelmingly by the Republicans
sort of supply side policies that came out

00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:00.019
of the 1980s.

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:05.790
Those would be my three kind of bits of advice
for Democrats to better appeal to rural voters.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:12.299
And the truth is that appealing to rural voters
in California versus Mississippi are certainly

00:03:12.299 --> 00:03:13.689
two different things.

00:03:13.689 --> 00:03:15.920
And and the Midwest as a third one.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:16.999
Those are my initial thoughts.

00:03:16.999 --> 00:03:18.780
Let me know what you think.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.379
We have a fantastic bonus show for you today.

